      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your concerns with specific compounds; certain filters might not be as effective against them. For better protection against organic aerosols and chemical compounds, look for specialized particulate air purifiers that come with activated carbon filters, designed to adsorb harsh chemicals and absorb volatile organic compounds (VOCs) emitted from substances like growth hormones. These filters are typically included in high-quality air filtration systems specifically marketed to combat these compounds embedded in mist or aerosols. It is also advised to conduct regular maintenance and replacements accordingly to ensure the effectiveness of these filters. In addition, thermal oxidizers can break down these compounds at high temperatures; however, this might not be feasible for residential use due to cost and complexity. Always check and research the specifications of each air purifier to ensure they meet your needs for filtering specific chemicals.",
